<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Palatinate-Neuburg</h1><p class="st-meta">1505 CE – 1742 CE · capital Neuburg an der Donau</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The 'Young Palatinate' on the Danube, created after the Landshut War, whose dukes inherited Jülich and Berg and then the Palatine electorate.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-cologne">Cologne</a> arbitration of 1505 that ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-landshut-succession">War of the Landshut Succession</a> created a new principality from parts of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-bavaria-landshut">Duchy of Bavaria-Landshut</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-henry-elector-palatine">Otto Henry</a> and Philip, the young sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rupert-of-germany">Rupert of the Palatinate</a>. Known as the Young <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/electoral-palatinate">Palatinate</a>, it had <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neuburg-an-der-donau">Neuburg</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> as its capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-henry-elector-palatine">Otto Henry</a> introduced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> in 1542 and rebuilt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neuburg-an-der-donau">Neuburg</a> castle in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> style before becoming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elector-palatine">Elector Palatine</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolfgang-william-count-palatine-of-neuburg">Wolfgang William</a> converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a> in 1613 to strengthen his claim in the Jülich succession and won Jülich and Berg, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dusseldorf">Düsseldorf</a>. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-william-elector-palatine">Philip William</a> became Elector Palatine in 1685, after which the Neuburg dukes ruled from Düsseldorf, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg">Heidelberg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mannheim">Mannheim</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When Elector <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iii-philip-elector-palatine">Charles Philip</a>, the last of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neuburg-an-der-donau">Neuburg</a> line, died in 1742, his lands passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-theodore-elector-of-bavaria">Charles Theodore</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/palatinate-sulzbach">Palatinate-Sulzbach</a>, who in 1777 also inherited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>. Neuburg was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-wittelsbach">Wittelsbach</a> lands of Bavaria.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/palatinate-neuburg.jpg" alt="Palatinate-Neuburg" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artistUnknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banner_of_Palatinate-Neuburg_(3%5E2).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1505 CE – 1742 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Neuburg an der Donau</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Otto Henry, Wolfgang William, Philip William</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism, then Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bavarian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pfalz-Neuburg, Duchy of Neuburg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1624&amp;focus=palatinate-neuburg" aria-label="Palatinate-Neuburg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4939 476 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Palatinate-Neuburg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-